# Build outputs.
_novo/

# The generated API page.  `novo doc` writes it here so you can read
# what the registry will serve; the registry gets its own copy,
# uploaded beside the archive by `novo pkg publish`.  It is generated
# from the sources, so committing it would be committing a second
# original.
APIDOC.md

# The built package binary.  This package is a LIBRARY and builds none;
# the line is here for when it grows a `main`.
/tera-nv

# The resolved dependency closure.  It is ignored HERE, and only here,
# because this package's one dependency is a sibling by path while the
# two are developed together — so the lock names a directory in this
# tree and would be wrong on every other machine.  It becomes a
# registry range at publish, and the lock becomes worth committing.
novo.lock
